      "value": "@{5aab30ea0b6da707273dbb98|full_name}: I know this is an old post, but I absolutely agree with this. Properly set up object spawns do not cause any significant lag. Even when a spawner for a properly set up prefab object is spammed (more than 5 spawns per second) the induced lag is barely noticeable, if at all, in my experience. \nWorld creators should be given more options, not less. Hardly justified to take this away from everyone for the mistakes of a few.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
